  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Suo Motu vs State Of Kerala on 27 June, 2024 Author: Anil K. Narendran Bench: Anil K.Narendran In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Anil K.Narendran & The Honourable Mr. Justice Harisankar V. Menon Thursday, the 27th day of June 2024 / 6th Ashadha, 1946 Sscr No. 17 Of 2024 In The Matter Of Travancore Devaswom Board - Sabarimala Special Commissioner Report-Sm.No.17/2024- Report Submitted By The Special Commissioner, Sabarimala Regarding The Hazards Caused To Wildlife Due To The Dumping Of Glass Soft Drink Bottles In And Around The Trek Paths, Pamba And Sannidhanam-Suo Motu Proceedings Initiated-Reg: ------------ Petitioner: Suo Motu Respondents: 1. State Of Kerala Represented By The Principal Secretary To Government, Revenue (Devaswom)Department, Government Secretariat, Thiruvananthapuram-695 001 2. THE TRAVANCORE DEVASWOM BOARD REPRESENTED BY ITS SECRETARY, NANTHANCODE, KAWDIAR POST, THIRUVANANTHAPURAM - 695 003. 3. THE DEVASWOM COMMISSIONER TRAVANCORE DEVASWOM BOARD, DEVASWOM BUILDINGS, NANTHANCODE, Suo Motu vs State Of Kerala on 27 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/2913527/ 1 THIRUVANANTHAPURAM, PIN-695 005 4. *DEPUTY DIRECTOR, PERIYAR TIGER RESERVE (WEST DIVISION), PEERUMEDU, IDUKKI-685531. *(DEPUTY DIRECTOR, PERIYAR WEST DIVISION CORRECTED AS ABOVE BY ORDER DATED 27/06/2024 IN SSCR NO.17/2024) 5. PRINCIPAL CHIEF CONSERVATOR OF FORESTS (WILDLIFE) & CHIEF WILDLIFE WARDEN, FOREST HEADQUARTERS, VAZHUTHACAUD, THIRUVANANTHAPURAM- 695014. 6. THE KERALA STATE POLLUTION CONTROL BOARD REPRESENTED BY ITS SECRETARY, HEAD OFFICE, PATTOM P.O., THIRUVANANTHAPURAM, PIN-695004. BY SRI.S.RAJMOHAN, SR.GOVERNMENT PLEADER BY SRI.NAGARAJ NARAYANAN, SPL.GOVERNMENT PLEADER (FOREST) BY STANDING COUNSEL FOR TRAVANCORE DEVASWOM BOARD BY STANDING COUNSEL FOR KERALA STATE POLLUTION CONTROL BOARD BY SMT.SAYUJYA RADHAKRISHNAN, AMICUS CURIAE FOR SABARIMALA SPL.COMMISSIONER THIS SABARIMALA SPECIAL COMMISSIONER REPORT HAVING COME UP FOR ORDERS AGAIN ON 27/06/2024, UPON PERUSING THE REPORT AND THIS COURT'S ORDER DATED 21/06/2024, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY PASSED THE FOLLOWING: ANNEXURES IN SSCR NO.17/2024 ANNEXURE 1: REPORT DATED 18/06/2024 SUBMITTED BY THE DEPUTY DIRECTOR, PERIYAR TIGER RESERVE WEST DIVISION. ANIL K. NARENDRAN & HARISANKAR V. MENON, JJ. ----------------------------------------------------- S.S.C.R. No.17 of 2024 -------------------------------------------------------- Suo Motu vs State Of Kerala on 27 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/2913527/ 2 Dated this the 27th day of June, 2024 ORDER Anil K. Narendran, J. The description of the 4th respondent is suo motu corrected as \"Deputy Director, Periyar Tiger Reserve (West Division), Peerumedu, Idukki-685531.\" On 21.06.2024, when this matter came for consideration, the learned Senior Government Pleader and the respective Standing Counsel for the Travancore Devaswom Board and the Kerala State Pollution Control Board sought time to get instructions.",
    "facts": "2. The Special Commissioner, Sabarimala, has filed this report regarding the hazards caused to wildlife due to the dumping of glass soft drink bottles in and around the trekking path to Sabarimala and Sannidhanam by Sabarimala pilgrims. By the order dated 21.02.2024, the learned Senior Government Pleader was directed to get instructions as to whether the sale of soft drinks in the Eco Shops by the Forest Department at Sabarimala is through soft drink dispenser machines.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
